1.Aim

Write a program to demostrate dictionary and related functions in python

2.Algorithm

1. Start the program.
2. Create a dictionary named emp with employee details.
3. Display the dictionary.
4. Access and display the values of name, age, sal, and dept.
5. Add a new key ph no to the dictionary.
6. Display the updated dictionary.
7. Update the value of sal.
8. Display the updated dictionary.
9. Delete the key dept.
10. Display the dictionary after deletion.
11. Display all keys, values, and items of the dictionary.
12. Use get() to retrieve the value of name.
13. Use get() to retrieve dept; if not found, display "not available".
14. Update age and ph no using the update() method.
15. Display the updated dictionary.
16. Accept a string from the user.
17. Create an empty dictionary called frequency.
18. For each character in the string, if the character already exists in frequency, increase its count by 1 or add the character with count 1.
19. Display the frequency of each character.
20. Stop the program.

3.Source Code 

# Dictionary creation

emp = {"name": "rahul", "age": 35, "sal": 50000, "dept": "IT"}
print("The dictionary is:", emp)

#accessing

print("name:", emp["name"])
print("age:", emp["age"])
print("salary: ", emp["sal"])
print("department:", emp["dept"])

#add,update,delete

emp["ph no"] = 9988776655
print("after adding:", emp)
emp["sal"] = 60000
print("after updating:", emp)
del emp["dept"]
print("after delesing: ", emp)

#methods

print("keys:")
print (emp.keys())
print ("values: ")
print(emp.values())
print("items")
print(emp.items())
print("name:", emp.get("name"))
print("dept:", emp.get("dept", "not available"))
emp.update({"age": 36, "ph no" : 8567849043})
print("after update")
print(emp)

#frequency

text = input("enter the strings: ")
frequency={}
for ch in text:
    if ch in frequency:
       frequency[ch] = frequency [ch]+1
    else:
       frequency[ch] = 1
print("Character Frequency")
for ch, count in frequency.items():
    print(ch,":", count)

